  "response": "생각이 맴돌면서 몸도 긴장되어 있다면, 잠들려고 노력할수록 더清醒해지는 악순환이 생기겠어요.\n\n3개월 전부터 시작됐다고 하셨는데, 그 무렵에 생활에 변화가 있었거나 마음이 쓰이는 일이 생겼을까요?",
  "reasoning": "The client is describing their sleep difficulty: it's been about 3 months, takes 1-2 hours to fall asleep (sometimes longer), and when they can't sleep, they ruminate on the day's events and feel physically tense.\n\nWhat would be helpful here? The client has shared that rumination and physical tension are present. I should:\n1. Validate what they've shared\n2. Gently explore further - maybe what kinds of thoughts keep coming up, or whether there's a pattern to when it started (3 months ago - did something happen then?)\n3. Not jump to solutions yet, but also not just keep asking the same type of questions\n\nI think a good next step would be to acknowledge the rumination pattern and gently explore whether something specific started around 3 months ago, since that could be relevant to understanding the root. Or I could explore the content of the thoughts - are they about specific concerns, or more general?\n\nI'll go with exploring what started around 3 months ago, since that's a concrete and useful piece of information that could help understand the trigger. I'll keep it gentle and not assume anything.\n",
